title: F_Duel_Roots
---
Chet Studwell: My roots are natural. Like my talent. And my tan. Point, Studwell!
Dex: Gloria's comeback doesn't fit anything Chet actually said. I'll save it for a guy with roots.
<<jump F_Duel_Lose>>
===
title: F_Duel_Lose
---
Chet Studwell: Ha! Weak. I've heard better comebacks from a vending machine. And it only says "exact change".
Roxy Vale: Ooh. That one goes to Chet, lover boy. Find better material and try again.
Dex: Each insult needs the comeback that answers it. Every woman in that audience has handled a guy like Chet. I should ask around.
===
title: F_Duel_Win
---
Roxy Vale: Five for five! Chet, sweetie, you look a little pale. Paler. Under the tan.
Chet Studwell: I... you... (slaps his ear) Come ON! My tape ALWAYS has the next line!
Roxy Vale: Your TAPE, Chet?
Chet Studwell: My... tapeworm. I have a very smart tapeworm.
Dex: You mean this tape? "CHET'S COMEBACKS. PLAY ON LOOP. CHANNEL CHET." In glitter pen. It was playing up in the booth, beamed to a walkie behind Camera One, beamed into your ear.
Roxy Vale: Chet Studwell! Hand over that earpiece. Now.
Chet Studwell: This is an outrage! My dad owns the network!
Roxy Vale: And I own this microphone. Earpiece. Hand. Now.
Dex: He drops a tiny earpiece into her palm. The audience boos him. Tess salutes me with her clipboard.
Roxy Vale: Your name is clear, lover boy. Sorry I doubted you. A little.
<<take chet_cheat_tape>>
<<flag f_chet_busted>>
===

title: F_Audience_Look
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: The whole audience is still here, chanting my name. Well, chanting "DEX-ish". Close enough.
<<else>>
    Dex: The studio audience. Lacey Rae, Ivy, Tess, Dolly, Mina, Sky, Bree, Lou, Mimi and Jett. They all came. For me.
    Dex: Somebody has a sign that says "GO DEX". Somebody else has a sign that says "WHO IS DEX". Fair.
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Audience_Talk
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Lacey Rae: Way to go, freshman!
    Ivy: (louder than ever) You were listening so hard. We all saw it.
    Tess Calloway: I've already scheduled the victory party. You're on the clipboard.
    Dex: Best. Night. Ever.
<<else>>
    Dex: Who should I talk to?
    -> Lacey Rae
        <<jump F_Lacey>>
    -> Ivy
        <<jump F_Ivy>>
    -> Tess Calloway
        <<jump F_Tess>>
    -> Dolly Spark
        <<jump F_Dolly>>
    -> Dr. Mina Volt
        <<jump F_Mina>>
    -> Sky Rivera
        <<jump F_Sky>>
    -> Bree Marlowe
        <<jump F_Bree>>
    -> Lou
        <<jump F_Lou>>
    -> Mimi
        <<jump F_Mimi>>
    -> Jett Vex
        <<jump F_Jett>>
    -> Never mind
        Dex: I'll just wave. They all wave back. I might cry.
<<endif>>
===

title: F_Lacey
---
<<if flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Lacey Rae: Freshman! You put that varmint in his place! I'm so proud I could yodel. I might yodel.
<<elseif not flagged("f_shirt_clean")>>
    Lacey Rae: Freshman! You wore the hat all the way to TV. But honey, that purple splotch...
<<else>>
    Lacey Rae: Freshman! You wore the hat all the way to TV. I'm so proud I could yodel.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
===
title: F_Lacey_Menu
---
-> What do I do about this stain? <<if not flagged("f_shirt_clean") and not flagged("f_lacey_stain")>>
    Lacey Rae: Ask a waitress, honey. They've seen every stain known to man. And a few known only to truckers.
    <<flag f_lacey_stain>>
    <<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
-> Chet's going to trash-talk me. Got anything? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_lacey")>>
    Lacey Rae: Oh, I know his type. Back home we had a fella like that at every barn dance. Always making fun of how other folks moved.
    Lacey Rae: If he says you dance like a folding chair, or a fence post, or anything that falls over, you tell him:
    Lacey Rae: "A folding chair still holds folks up. When's the last time you did that?"
    Dex: A folding chair holds folks up. Got it. That's for when he makes fun of my dancing.
    <<flag f_cb_lacey>>
    <<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
-> Tell me that comeback again? <<if flagged("f_cb_lacey") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Lacey Rae: When he knocks your dancing: "A folding chair still holds folks up. When's the last time you did that?"
    <<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
-> Any tips for the dance-off?
    Lacey Rae: Boots heavy, heart light. Heel, toe, scoot, and tip the hat. Do that, and nobody can touch you.
    <<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
-> Still listening to Hank Hollister? <<if not flagged("f_lacey_hank")>>
    Lacey Rae: Every day. I brought his album tonight. I bring it everywhere. It's basically a support animal.
    <<flag f_lacey_hank>>
    <<jump F_Lacey_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Lacey Rae: Go get 'em, freshman!
===

title: F_Ivy
---
Ivy: (whispering) Hi. It's loud in here. I'm wearing the sunglasses again.
<<jump F_Ivy_Menu>>
===
title: F_Ivy_Menu
---
-> Have you noticed anything about Chet? <<if not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    <<if flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
        Ivy: (whispering) He's just tapping his ear now. Nothing comes back. Without the voice, he's empty. Make him talk.
    <<elseif flagged("f_took_walkie")>>
        Ivy: (whispering) That walkie was just the middle. He keeps glancing up at that dark window over the green room door. Like a puppy waiting for its owner.
    <<else>>
        Ivy: (whispering) Quiet people notice things. He's getting lines from somewhere. Wireless ones.
        Ivy: (whispering) Before you came in, he stood behind that camera for a long time. Way too long for a guy who isn't a camera.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump F_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Chet's going to trash-talk me. Any ideas? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_ivy")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) People who brag about their trophies never have anybody listening to them. That's why they brag.
    Ivy: (whispering) If he brags about his trophies, tell him: "Must be quiet in there. The trophies are the only ones who'll listen to you."
    Dex: Trophies are the only ones who'll listen. For when he brags about his trophies. Ivy, that's brutal.
    Ivy: (whispering) Poets are brutal. We just say it quietly.
    <<flag f_cb_ivy>>
    <<jump F_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Tell me that comeback again? <<if flagged("f_cb_ivy") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) When he brags about trophies: "Must be quiet in there. The trophies are the only ones who'll listen to you."
    <<jump F_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Writing anything new? <<if not flagged("f_ivy_poem")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) A new poem. "Ode to the Boy in the Loud Shirt Who Was Kind to Everybody." It's a working title.
    Dex: That's... nice. Who's it about?
    Ivy: (whispering) ...You're very bad at poems.
    <<flag f_ivy_poem>>
    <<jump F_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Ivy: (whispering) Whatever happens, you got me to read a poem in public. That's already a miracle.
===

title: F_Tess
---
<<if flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Tess Calloway: I've drawn up a cheering schedule. Row two goes "Dex!", row three goes "Dooley!". Efficiency.
<<else>>
    Tess Calloway: Dex! I organised the whole audience. Seating chart, banners, a backup banner. And a backup for the backup.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
===
title: F_Tess_Menu
---
-> What's in the big folder? <<if not flagged("f_tess_log")>>
    Tess Calloway: The studio's equipment log. It was lying around. Unsupervised. So naturally I took charge of it, and everything clipped to it.
    Tess Calloway: If you need anything checked, signed or confiscated, I'm your girl.
    <<flag f_tess_log>>
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> Does the log say anything about this walkie? <<if (has("studio_walkie") or flagged("f_roxy_saw_walkie")) and not flagged("f_tess_walkie")>>
    Tess Calloway: (flips pages) Walkie number two. Signed out by C. Studwell. Reason: "winning".
    Tess Calloway: And on the same line: one tape deck and transmitter, CONTROL BOOTH. Same signature. Same glitter pen. Amateur hour.
    Dex: So whatever's feeding him lines is up in the control booth.
    <<flag f_tess_walkie>>
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> Is there anything in there for a runner called Kevin? <<if flagged("f_booth_refused") and not flagged("f_got_lanyard")>>
    Tess Calloway: Kevin... Kevin... here. "Runner: Kevin. Crew lanyard: NOT COLLECTED. Status: no-show." Unacceptable.
    Tess Calloway: His lanyard's still clipped to the log. You want it? Of course you want it. I'll make a note. "Kevin: replaced by Dex."
    Dex: She hands me a blue lanyard that says CREW: KEVIN. ALL ACCESS. I've never been all access. I've barely been some access.
    <<give runner_lanyard>>
    <<flag f_got_lanyard>>
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> Chet's going to trash-talk me. Got anything? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: Chet's going to say everybody came to see him. He said it to me at the door. Twice. He tried to sign my clipboard.
    Tess Calloway: When he does, tell him: "Funny. Tess made the seating chart, and you're listed under Fire Exit."
    Tess Calloway: It's true, by the way. I put him there. It's on the chart. The chart is laminated.
    <<flag f_cb_tess>>
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> Tell me that comeback again? <<if flagged("f_cb_tess") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Tess Calloway: When he says everybody came to see him: "Funny. Tess made the seating chart, and you're listed under Fire Exit."
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> How's Fernanda? <<if not flagged("f_tess_fernanda")>>
    Tess Calloway: Back on the porch, fully inflated, under twenty-four-hour guard. The guard is also a flamingo. Smaller. Inflatable. Very loyal.
    <<flag f_tess_fernanda>>
    <<jump F_Tess_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Tess Calloway: Don't be late for your cue. I will know.
===

title: F_Dolly
---
<<if flagged("f_track_ready")>>
    Dolly Spark: That mix is gonna blow the roof off. Not the fuse, though. I've learned my lesson.
<<elseif flagged("f_dolly_helped")>>
    Dolly Spark: Your tape's ready, babe. Pop it in the sound board.
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: Dex! Glow sticks for everybody!
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Dolly_Menu>>
