title: F_Dolly_Menu
---
-> Seen the sound board? <<if not flagged("f_saw_decks")>>
    Dolly Spark: Have YOU? I don't trust a dance-off I didn't DJ. Go check what's loaded in those decks.
    <<jump F_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Chet jammed his own tape in my deck! <<if flagged("f_saw_decks") and not flagged("f_dolly_helped") and not flagged("f_dolly_crime")>>
    Dolly Spark: Chet loaded his own tape in BOTH dance-off decks? That's not DJing, that's a crime.
    Dolly Spark: Bring me any tape. Even a terrible one. I'll record right over it with a mix that'll make you dance like nobody's grading.
    <<flag f_dolly_crime>>
    <<jump F_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Could you mix me a track on this? <<if has("chet_mixtape")>>
    <<jump F_Audience_Mixtape>>
-> Can I borrow your headphones? <<if flagged("f_booth_refused") and not flagged("f_lent_cans")>>
    Dolly Spark: My cans? For a DISGUISE? Babe, that's the most rock and roll thing anyone's ever asked me.
    Dolly Spark: Bring 'em back, though. I can't mix without them. A DJ without cans is just a girl pointing at buttons.
    <<give dolly_headphones>>
    <<flag f_lent_cans>>
    <<jump F_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Here are your headphones back. <<if has("runner_disguise") and flagged("f_tape_swapped") and not flagged("f_cans_back")>>
    <<jump F_Audience_Cans>>
-> How's the Fuse Box? <<if not flagged("f_dolly_fuse")>>
    Dolly Spark: Brand-new fuse, brand-new amp, and a sign over the decks: DROP THE BASS GENTLY. Nobody reads it. Least of all me.
    <<flag f_dolly_fuse>>
    <<jump F_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Dolly Spark: Later, babe! Keep it funky!
===

title: F_Mina
---
<<if flagged("f_miked")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: Your mic is reading strong. I can hear your heart rate from here. It's... elevated.
<<else>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: Professor Nibbles says hello. He's in my coat pocket. He's not technically allowed in here.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Mina_Menu>>
===
title: F_Mina_Menu
---
-> This mic pack's dead. Got a battery? <<if has("lapel_mic") and not flagged("f_mina_tip")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: Let me see. Hmm. Standard nine-volt clip, empty. Classic.
    Dr. Mina Volt: I always carry spares, but I gave my last one to Sky for her megaphone. She owes me. Ask her.
    <<flag f_mina_tip>>
    <<jump F_Mina_Menu>>
-> Could Professor Nibbles help me with something? <<if flagged("f_norma_guards") and not flagged("f_tape_swapped") and not has("nibbles_on_loan")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: A mission? He'd love that. He's been so bored since retirement. He's taken up knitting. Badly.
    Dr. Mina Volt: But he's a professional, Dex. He doesn't leave this pocket for less than one cheese puff. Union rules.
    Dex: Somewhere in this building there must be a snack table.
    <<flag f_mina_offer>>
    <<jump F_Mina_Menu>>
-> Here, a cheese puff. <<if has("studio_cheese_puff")>>
    <<jump F_Audience_CheesePuff>>
-> Any science tips for live TV? <<if not flagged("f_mina_science")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: Fun fact: TV studios eat batteries. And the lights run so hot that you lose a whole glass of sweat per hour. Hydrate.
    Dex: I did not need to know that.
    Dr. Mina Volt: Nobody does. That's what makes it science.
    <<flag f_mina_science>>
    <<jump F_Mina_Menu>>
-> How's the Professor's retirement? <<if not flagged("f_mina_nibbles")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: Wonderful. He has a little desk now, with a little nameplate. He mostly sleeps on it. Like a real professor.
    <<flag f_mina_nibbles>>
    <<jump F_Mina_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Dr. Mina Volt: Good luck! Statistically, you need it!
===

title: F_Sky
---
<<if flagged("f_sky_helped")>>
    Sky Rivera: (holding up her sign) WHAT DO WE WANT? DEX TO WIN! WHEN DO WE WANT IT? AFTER THE COMMERCIAL BREAK!
<<else>>
    Sky Rivera: I'm here to support you. And to protest Chet. Mostly to protest Chet.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Sky_Menu>>
===
title: F_Sky_Menu
---
-> Mina says you've got her spare battery. <<if flagged("f_mina_tip") and not flagged("f_sky_helped") and not flagged("f_sky_wants_sign")>>
    Sky Rivera: The nine-volt in my megaphone? Dex, man, this megaphone is my VOICE. Tonight I'm protesting Chet. Loudly.
    Sky Rivera: ...Unless. Unless I had a sign. A sign is a voice you don't have to charge. Mimi says silent protests hit the hardest.
    Sky Rivera: Bring me a protest sign. Big letters. Something about Chet. And then the battery's yours.
    <<flag f_sky_wants_sign>>
    <<jump F_Sky_Menu>>
-> What kind of sign do you want? <<if flagged("f_sky_wants_sign") and not flagged("f_sky_helped") and not has("chet_protest_sign")>>
    Sky Rivera: Something to write on and something bold to write with. Red's the colour of revolution. And of lipstick, I guess.
    <<jump F_Sky_Menu>>
-> Here's your protest sign. <<if has("chet_protest_sign")>>
    <<jump F_Audience_Sign>>
-> What else are you protesting tonight? <<if not flagged("f_sky_lore")>>
    Sky Rivera: Six-dollar studio water. Chet's teeth, which are an environmental hazard. And the APPLAUSE sign. Applause should be FREE.
    <<flag f_sky_lore>>
    <<jump F_Sky_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Sky Rivera: Power to the people, Dex!
===

title: F_Bree
---
<<if flagged("f_shirt_clean")>>
    Bree Marlowe: Look at you, camera-ready! Now hit your mark and find your light. Actor stuff.
<<else>>
    Bree Marlowe: Oh, honey. Is that grape soda? I've had worse dumped on me by the lunch rush.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Bree_Menu>>
===
title: F_Bree_Menu
---
-> Can you help me with this stain? <<if not flagged("f_bree_tip") and not flagged("f_shirt_clean")>>
    Bree Marlowe: Club soda on a napkin. Blot, don't rub. Here, I never go anywhere without napkins in my apron.
    Bree Marlowe: As for club soda, Lou brought a whole bag of drinks from the store. Studio prices offend her.
    <<give cocktail_napkin>>
    <<flag f_bree_tip>>
    <<jump F_Bree_Menu>>
-> Where do I get club soda again? <<if flagged("f_bree_tip") and not flagged("f_lou_helped")>>
    Bree Marlowe: Lou. Bag of drinks. Ask nicely, and only once.
    <<jump F_Bree_Menu>>
-> Can I borrow that pencil in your bun? <<if flagged("f_knows_rewind") and not flagged("f_got_pencil")>>
    Bree Marlowe: My order pencil? That pencil has taken ten thousand orders. It's seen things.
    Bree Marlowe: For you, sure. (she pulls it out and her whole bun falls down) ...Worth it. Go.
    <<give bun_pencil>>
    <<flag f_got_pencil>>
    <<jump F_Bree_Menu>>
-> How did the audition go? <<if not flagged("f_bree_lore")>>
    Bree Marlowe: It's tomorrow! But the casting lady saw my headshots and said, quote, "Who is your photographer?" I said, quote, "A freshman."
    <<flag f_bree_lore>>
    <<jump F_Bree_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Bree Marlowe: Break a leg! Not literally, we're short a waitress.
===

title: F_Lou
---
<<if flagged("f_lou_helped")>>
    Lou: I'm not smiling. My face is just tired from not smiling.
<<else>>
    Lou: I brought my own drinks. The studio charges six bucks a water. Criminals.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Lou_Menu>>
===
title: F_Lou_Menu
---
-> Could I have a club soda? For the stain. <<if flagged("f_bree_tip") and not flagged("f_lou_helped")>>
    Lou: Club soda. For the stain. Fine.
    Lou: You finished my crossword. I owe you one. This is the one. Don't make it weird.
    Dex: She hands me a bottle of club soda. Her mouth twitches. Was that... no. Couldn't be.
    <<give soda_water>>
    <<flag f_lou_helped>>
    <<jump F_Lou_Menu>>
-> Chet's going to trash-talk me. Any advice? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_lou")>>
    Lou: He flashed his teeth at me in the lobby. Said they're so white they've got their own lighting crew.
    Lou: If he says it to you: "Nice teeth. Shame nothing smart ever comes out between them."
    Lou: Don't smile when you say it. Smiling's for amateurs.
    <<flag f_cb_lou>>
    <<jump F_Lou_Menu>>
-> Tell me that comeback again? <<if flagged("f_cb_lou") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Lou: Teeth. "Nice teeth. Shame nothing smart ever comes out between them." Don't ask a third time.
    <<jump F_Lou_Menu>>
-> Started a new crossword? <<if not flagged("f_lou_lore")>>
    Lou: Yes. Seven down: "Contestant who will lose tonight." Five letters. Starts with C.
    Dex: ...Chet's only four letters.
    Lou: I write big.
    <<flag f_lou_lore>>
    <<jump F_Lou_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Lou: If you need something, ask. Don't ask twice.
===

title: F_Mimi
---
Dex: Mimi waves at me. Then she waves at an invisible person next to me. Then she makes the invisible person wave back.
<<jump F_Mimi_Menu>>
===
title: F_Mimi_Menu
---
-> What's Chet up to? <<if not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    <<if flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
        Dex: Mimi mimes Chet slapping his ear. Then mimes an empty speech bubble. Then pops it. She's having the time of her life.
    <<elseif flagged("f_took_walkie")>>
        Dex: Mimi points up at the dark window over the green room door. She mimes headphones, then pressing PLAY, then a little tape going round and round.
        Dex: Somebody up in the booth is playing a tape. For Chet. Got it.
    <<else>>
        Dex: Mimi points at Chet. Then at her ear. Then she mimes cranking an old-timey radio and pretends to tape it to something big with a lens.
        Dex: She's saying... Chet has a radio taped to... a camera? Or an elephant. I really hope it's a camera.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump F_Mimi_Menu>>
-> Got any comebacks for Chet? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Dex: Mimi zips her lips and throws away the key. Then she picks the key back up, unlocks her lips, and points firmly at Jett.
    Dex: So: mimes don't do comebacks. Punk rockers do. Ask Jett.
    <<jump F_Mimi_Menu>>
-> How's the invisible box? <<if not flagged("f_mimi_box")>>
    Dex: Mimi mimes unlocking the box with a key, stepping out, and then, very slowly, building a small invisible porch onto it.
    Dex: She's renovating. Good for her.
    <<flag f_mimi_box>>
    <<jump F_Mimi_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Dex: Mimi mimes a giant trophy. Then mimes handing it to me. Then mimes crying with joy. She's a lot.
===

title: F_Jett
---
<<if flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Jett Vex: You took down Chet. On live TV. That was almost punk.
<<else>>
    Jett Vex: Bored. ...Okay, a little less bored than usual. Don't let it go to your head.
<<endif>>
<<jump F_Jett_Menu>>
===
title: F_Jett_Menu
---
-> Chet's going to trash-talk me. Help? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_jett")>>
    Jett Vex: Guys like Chet always end the same way. "Nobody's going to remember your name." Yawn.
    Jett Vex: So forget HIS name right back. "Sorry, what was your name again? Chad? Chip? Chuck?"
    Jett Vex: Nothing hurts a Chet more than not being remembered. It's like stepping on a guitar pedal that's off.
    <<flag f_cb_jett>>
    <<jump F_Jett_Menu>>
-> Tell me that comeback again? <<if flagged("f_cb_jett") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Jett Vex: When he says nobody will remember you: "Sorry, what was your name again? Chad? Chip? Chuck?" Deadpan. No smile.
    <<jump F_Jett_Menu>>
-> Check out Chet's mixtape. <<if has("chet_mixtape")>>
    Jett Vex: "Pump-Up Jams Volume 9: Songs About Chet." Wow. That's so bad it's almost punk.
    Jett Vex: Almost. Give it to Dolly. Let her record over it before it hurts somebody.
    <<jump F_Jett_Menu>>
-> Will you dance tonight? <<if not flagged("f_jett_lore")>>
    Jett Vex: If that dance-off gets lame, I'm leaving. So don't let it get lame.
    Dex: No pressure.
    Jett Vex: All the pressure. That's what makes it fun.
    <<flag f_jett_lore>>
    <<jump F_Jett_Menu>>
-> Talk to someone else
    <<jump F_Audience_Talk>>
-> See you later
    Jett Vex: Whatever. ...Good luck. Ugh.
===

title: F_Audience_Mixtape
---
<<if flagged("f_dolly_helped")>>
    Dolly Spark: I already made you a tape, babe.
<<elseif not flagged("f_tape_wound")>>
    Dolly Spark: Babe, half this tape is hanging out like spaghetti. Chet must've yanked it. I can't record on spaghetti.
    Dolly Spark: Old DJ trick: stick a pencil in the little hole and twirl it back in. Twirl, twirl, twirl.
    Dex: A pencil. Who brings a pencil to a TV show? Somebody who takes orders all day... Bree keeps one stuck in her bun!
    <<flag f_knows_rewind>>
<<elseif flagged("f_lent_cans") and not flagged("f_cans_back")>>
    Dolly Spark: Love the tape. But I can't mix without my headphones, and right now they're busy being Kevin.
    Dolly Spark: Finish your sneaky business, then bring 'em back.
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: Chet's tape? Perfect. Recording over it is the nicest thing anyone could do for it.
    Dolly Spark: (slams it into a tiny boombox, slides her headphones on) One... two... and DROP!
    Jett Vex: Ugh. That's actually good. I hate it. Turn it up.
    Dolly Spark: Done. "Dolly's Floor-Fillers, Dex Edition." Track one: Disco Volcano. Obviously. Put it in the sound board and dance like the fuse can't blow.
    <<take chet_mixtape>>
    <<give floor_fillers_tape>>
    <<flag f_dolly_helped>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Audience_Cans
---
<<if flagged("f_cans_back")>>
    Dolly Spark: I've already got my cans back, babe.
<<elseif not flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Dolly Spark: My cans! On your head, with a straw! You look like a very confused pilot. Keep 'em till you're done sneaking around, babe.
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: My cans! I'll take those. You can keep the straw. And the lanyard. Hi, Kevin.
    Dex: I'm not Kevin any more. Kevin had a good run. Kevin is at peace.
    <<take runner_disguise>>
    <<flag f_cans_back>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Audience_CansEarly
---
Dolly Spark: My headphones? Keep 'em till you've done your sneaky thing, babe. Just don't sit on them.
===
title: F_Audience_CheesePuff
---
<<if has("nibbles_on_loan")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: The Professor's already with you, Dex. Mission first, snacks after.
<<elseif flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: For me? Thanks! (crunch) Nibbles is asleep. He did a big mission tonight. He won't tell me what.
    <<take studio_cheese_puff>>
<<elseif flagged("f_norma_guards") or flagged("f_mina_offer")>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: A cheese puff! Professor Nibbles' one true weakness. He's out of my pocket already. Look at him go.
    Dr. Mina Volt: Where he goes, he'll do his job and come straight back to me. He always does. He's very professional.
    Dex: Professor Nibbles, on loan, in a paper cup. He's chewing the cheese puff and looking at me like a tiny action hero.
    <<take studio_cheese_puff>>
    <<give nibbles_on_loan>>
<<else>>
    Dr. Mina Volt: For me? Thanks! (crunch) Nibbles is jealous. He'd do anything for one of those, you know. Anything.
    <<take studio_cheese_puff>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Audience_Nibbles
---
Dr. Mina Volt: Professor! Not yet, he's on a mission. Go, go! He'll come back to me when the job's done.
===
title: F_Audience_Sign
---
Sky Rivera: A protest sign! In Scandal Red! "CHET IS A CHEAT"! It's beautiful. It's silent. It's devastating.
Sky Rivera: Mimi was right. The quiet ones hit the hardest. Here: one nine-volt, liberated from the megaphone.
Dex: She pops the battery out and holds the sign up high. Chet sees it and pretends he can't read. Which, honestly, might be true.
<<take chet_protest_sign>>
<<give nine_volt>>
<<flag f_sky_helped>>
===
title: F_Audience_CheatTape
---
Dolly Spark: Record over Chet's cheat tape? Tempting, babe. But that's evidence. Roxy'll want it.
===
title: F_Audience_Walkie
---
Tess Calloway: Dex! A walkie-talkie? Before you go waving that around, talk to me. I have paperwork.
===
title: F_Audience_Mic
---
Dr. Mina Volt: Is that a dead mic pack? Bring it over, let me take a look. Talk to me!
===
title: F_Audience_Item
---
Dex: They cheer at it politely. They'd cheer at anything I held up right now. It's nice.
===

title: F_Camera_Look
---
Dex: Camera One. It's pointed at the stage, and it's bigger than my whole dorm room.
===
title: F_Camera_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_took_walkie")>>
    Dex: I look through the viewfinder. Everyone looks better on camera. Except Chet. Chet looks the same.
<<else>>
    Dex: On the back of the camera, hidden under a pile of cables: a walkie-talkie, taped down. CHET is written on it in glitter pen.
    Walkie-talkie: (crackle) ...Chet, it's you. From earlier. Remember: smile, lie, repeat. Over.
    Dex: That's Chet's voice. A recording of Chet, feeding Chet his lines. Through the earpiece!
    Dex: The walkie's little screen says RECEIVING FROM: BOOTH. So it's just a relay. The tape must be playing somewhere upstairs.
    <<give studio_walkie>>
    <<flag f_took_walkie>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_Board_Look
---
Dex: The sound board. Two decks, labelled "DANCE-OFF: CONTESTANT 1" and "DANCE-OFF: CONTESTANT 2".
===
title: F_Board_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_track_ready")>>
    Dex: Dolly's mix is cued up in deck two. I'm not touching anything else. Too many buttons.
<<elseif flagged("f_ejected")>>
    Dex: Deck two is empty. I need my own dance-off track to put in it.
<<else>>
    Dex: Deck one: "Chet's Pump-Up Jams, Volume 9". Deck two: ALSO "Chet's Pump-Up Jams, Volume 9", jammed in sideways. He loaded his tape in my deck!
    Dex: (yank) It comes out trailing a mile of brown tape, like spaghetti. Sabotage!
    Dex: Now my deck's empty. I'll need something to put in it.
    <<give chet_mixtape>>
    <<flag f_ejected>>
    <<flag f_saw_decks>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Board_Tape
---
Dex: Dolly's mix, into deck two. Click. It even sounds good just sitting there.
<<take floor_fillers_tape>>
<<flag f_track_ready>>
===
title: F_Board_ChetTape
---
Dex: Put Chet's tape back in my deck? No thank you. "Songs About Chet" is not a dance-off strategy.
===
title: F_Board_CheatTape
---
Dex: Chet's Comebacks as my dance-off music? Track one: an insult. Track two: the same insult, slower. Pass.
===

title: F_Applause_Look
---
Dex: An APPLAUSE sign. The most powerful object in television.
===
title: F_Applause_Use
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: I flick the APPLAUSE sign on. The audience gives me a standing ovation. Again. Okay, one more time.
<<else>>
    Dex: I flick it on. The whole audience cheers. Lou does not cheer. Lou nods, which for Lou is a parade.
<<endif>>
===

title: F_Mark_Look
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: My contestant mark. Somebody's already drawn a little star on it.
<<else>>
    Dex: A taped X on the floor with "DEX" written on it. Wait, no, it says "DEC". Close enough.
<<endif>>
===
title: F_Mark_Use
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: I stand on my mark one more time. No cameras, no lights. Just me and the memory of the greatest dance-off of all time.
<<elseif flagged("f_miked") and flagged("f_shirt_clean") and flagged("f_track_ready") and flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Dex: I step onto my mark. Roxy nods. The red light flicks on.
    <<jump F_Show>>
<<elseif not flagged("f_met_roxy")>>
    Dex: I should check in with the host before I start standing on things.
<<else>>
    Dex: I step on the mark. Nothing happens. I'm not ready yet. Let me think...
    <<jump F_Hints>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_Combine_Mic
---
Dex: Battery in. Click. A tiny green light! I clip the mic to my collar. "Testing, testing." It works!
Dr. Mina Volt: (from the audience) Science!
<<take lapel_mic>>
<<take nine_volt>>
<<flag f_miked>>
===
title: F_Combine_Blot
---
Dex: Club soda on the napkin. Blot. Don't rub. Blot. Blot...
Dex: The purple fades away. My hibiscus are back! ...And now there's a huge soggy patch right in the middle. I look like I lost a water-balloon fight.
Dex: Roxy is not going to allow "damp" on her show. I need to dry this. Fast.
<<take soda_water>>
<<take cocktail_napkin>>
<<unflag f_shirt_stained>>
<<flag f_shirt_wet>>
===
title: F_Combine_Sign
---
Dex: I flip Chet's RESERVED card over. Blank on the back. Perfect.
Dex: In big Scandal Red letters: CHET IS A CHEAT. I add a little drawing of his teeth. They look terrifying. Accurate.
<<take reserved_card>>
<<take scandal_lipstick>>
<<give chet_protest_sign>>
===
title: F_Combine_Headset
---
Dex: Dolly's headphones on my head. Bendy straw tucked into the left earcup, bent round in front of my mouth. A microphone arm!
Dex: It's a crew headset. A crew headset that smells faintly of strawberry milk.
<<take dolly_headphones>>
<<take bendy_straw>>
<<give crew_headset>>
<<flag f_made_headset>>
===
title: F_Combine_Disguise
---
Dex: Headset on. Lanyard round my neck: CREW: KEVIN. ALL ACCESS. I tuck my hibiscus collar in and try to look tired and underpaid.
Dex: I am Kevin. Kevin is me. Together, we are The Kevin Kit.
<<take crew_headset>>
<<take runner_lanyard>>
<<give runner_disguise>>
===
title: F_Combine_Rewind
---
Dex: Pencil in the little hole. Twirl. Twirl. Twirl, twirl, twirl...
Dex: The brown spaghetti slurps back into the cassette. Good as new. Well, bad as new. It's still "Songs About Chet".
Dex: Bree's pencil is now permanently bent. I'll buy her a new one. A whole box. With a bow.
<<take bun_pencil>>
<<flag f_tape_wound>>
===

title: F_GR_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("f_gr_intro")>>
    Dex: The green room. A couch, a mirror with about a hundred light bulbs, a snack table, and a rack of clothes that sparkles at me threateningly.
    Gloria Puff: Well, look at you. A walking fruit basket. I'm Gloria Puff, sugar. Hair, makeup, wardrobe and emotional support.
    Gloria Puff: Nobody goes on camera without passing through my chair first. Nobody.
    Dex: At the back, a narrow door: CREW ONLY. CONTROL BOOTH. There's an intercom next to it with a big red TALK button.
    <<flag f_gr_intro>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_GR_Exit_Look
---
Dex: The door back out to the studio. I can hear Tess organising the audience through it.
===
title: F_GR_Exit_Use
---
<<go tv_studio from_green_room>>
===

title: F_GR_Craft_Look
---
Dex: Craft services. A bowl of cheese puffs, a cup of bendy straws, and one eclair with a bite out of it.
Dex: The eclair has a sticky note: CHET'S. DO NOT TOUCH. LICKED.
===
title: F_GR_Craft_Use
---
Dex: What should I grab?
-> A cheese puff <<if not has("studio_cheese_puff")>>
    Dex: One cheese puff. Neon orange. It leaves a mark on my fingers that will outlive me.
    <<give studio_cheese_puff>>
-> A bendy straw <<if not has("bendy_straw") and not flagged("f_made_headset")>>
    Dex: A pink bendy straw. Bendy straws make every drink a party. I don't have a drink. I'll find a use for it.
    <<give bendy_straw>>
-> Chet's eclair
    Dex: The note says LICKED. I'm going to trust the note.
-> Nothing
    Dex: I'm too nervous to eat. That's a first.
===
title: F_GR_Craft_Item
---
Dex: I put it back. Then I take it again. Snack tables are a one-way street.
===

title: F_Rack_Look
---
Dex: The wardrobe rack. Sequin jackets, feather boas, and a T-shirt with a tuxedo printed on it. There's a box of mic packs on the bottom.
===
title: F_Rack_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_took_mic") or flagged("f_miked")>>
    Dex: I tried on a feather boa. It tried on me back. I'm leaving it.
<<elseif not flagged("f_made_up")>>
    Gloria Puff: Ah-ah-ah! Hands off my rack, sugar. Wardrobe is for talent, and talent goes through my chair first.
    Dex: Even the mic packs?
    Gloria Puff: ESPECIALLY the mic packs. Nobody gets wired up looking like a glazed ham.
<<else>>
    Gloria Puff: Go on, sugar. You're powdered. You've earned it.
    Dex: A box marked "MIC PACKS". All of them are dead. Of course they are. I'll take one anyway.
    <<give lapel_mic>>
    <<flag f_took_mic>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_GR_Sign_Look
---
Dex: A little brass stand with a card in it: RESERVED: C. STUDWELL. ALL NIGHT. He's not even here. He's out there winking at a camera.
===
title: F_GR_Sign_Use
---
Dex: I slide the card out of the little stand. Whoops. It must have fallen. Into my pocket.
Gloria Puff: (not looking up) I didn't see that. I see nothing. I'm a makeup artist, not a witness.
Dex: The back of the card is completely blank. Chet doesn't even use both sides of things.
<<give reserved_card>>
<<flag f_took_card>>
===

title: F_GR_Chair_Look
---
<<if flagged("f_took_card")>>
    Dex: A big leather makeup chair facing a mirror ringed with light bulbs. It's free. It's waiting for me. It looks hungry.
<<else>>
    Dex: A big leather makeup chair facing a mirror ringed with light bulbs. Next to it, a little sign: RESERVED: C. STUDWELL.
<<endif>>
===
title: F_GR_Chair_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_shirt_wet")>>
    <<jump F_GR_Dry>>
<<elseif flagged("f_made_up")>>
    Gloria Puff: Sit any longer, sugar, and I'll start on your eyebrows. Nobody wants that. Least of all your eyebrows.
<<elseif not flagged("f_took_card")>>
    Gloria Puff: That chair is reserved, sugar. Mister Studwell booked it for the whole night. Nobody sits while that little sign's up. House rules.
    Dex: The chair's empty, though. He's not coming back. He's busy being Chet.
    Gloria Puff: If that sign went missing, it'd be first come, first powdered. I'm just saying. I'm saying nothing. I'm saying it loudly.
<<else>>
    <<jump F_GR_Makeup>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_GR_Chair_Card
---
Dex: Put Chet's card back? That's the opposite of progress.
===
title: F_GR_Makeup
---
Gloria Puff: The sign's gone? Then sit, sugar. First come, first powdered.
Dex: I sit. She attacks. Powder. Brushes. Something cold. Something that smells like a cupcake. Something that I'm pretty sure was a tiny sponge.
Gloria Puff: Hold still. Chin up. Chin down. Stop blinking. Who taught you to blink like that?
Dex: She spins the chair around to the mirror. I look... good? I look like me, but I slept eight hours and drink water.
Gloria Puff: There. Now you're talent. Wardrobe's open to you, mic packs included.
<<if flagged("f_shirt_stained")>>
    Gloria Puff: That purple blob, though? Not my department. I do faces. Stains are wet work. Get it wet and my Turbo-Puff 3000 will dry it before the commercial.
    <<flag f_asked_gloria_stain>>
<<endif>>
<<flag f_made_up>>
===
title: F_GR_Dry
---
Gloria Puff: Sugar, you're DRIPPING on my floor. Arms up! Turbo-Puff 3000, full blast!
Dex: WHOOOOOSH. It's like standing behind a jet engine that loves me.
Dex: Ten seconds later my shirt is dry, warm and somehow fluffier than when I bought it. The hibiscus are back and they're thriving.
Gloria Puff: Camera-ready. Go knock 'em dead. Not literally, we don't have the insurance.
<<unflag f_shirt_wet>>
<<flag f_shirt_clean>>
===

title: F_GR_Gloria_Look
---
Dex: Gloria Puff. A platinum beehive tall enough to have its own weather, a smock full of brushes, and a powder puff the size of a cat.
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Talk
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Gloria Puff: Sugar, you were glowing out there. That was my powder. Also you. Mostly my powder.
<<elseif flagged("f_shirt_wet")>>
    Gloria Puff: Sugar, why are you wet? Never mind. Don't tell me. Come here.
<<elseif flagged("f_made_up")>>
    Gloria Puff: There's my handsome canvas. Don't touch your face. I can feel you thinking about touching your face.
<<else>>
    Gloria Puff: Back again, sugar? You're still shiny. I can see my reflection in your forehead.
<<endif>>
<<if not flagged("finale_won")>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Menu
---
-> Can I sit in your chair? <<if not flagged("f_made_up")>>
    <<jump F_GR_Chair_Use>>
-> Can you dry my shirt? <<if flagged("f_shirt_wet")>>
    <<jump F_GR_Dry>>
-> Could I borrow a lipstick? <<if flagged("f_sky_wants_sign") and not flagged("f_got_lipstick")>>
    Gloria Puff: A lipstick? For a protest sign? Against CHET? Sugar, I have been waiting for this day my whole career.
    Gloria Puff: Scandal Red. Discontinued for being too scandalous. Write big.
    <<give scandal_lipstick>>
    <<flag f_got_lipstick>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> Can you do anything about this purple stain? <<if not flagged("f_shirt_clean") and not flagged("f_shirt_wet") and not flagged("f_asked_gloria_stain")>>
    Gloria Puff: Grape soda? Not my department, sugar. I do faces. Stains are wet work.
    Gloria Puff: But you get that shirt wet, and my Turbo-Puff 3000 will have it bone dry before the commercial.
    <<flag f_asked_gloria_stain>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> What's the director like? <<if not flagged("f_asked_norma")>>
    Gloria Puff: Norma Fade. Up in the booth. Thirty years of live TV. Tough as a two-dollar steak.
    Gloria Puff: She's scared of exactly one thing in this world: rodents. A mouse ran across the set once and she directed a whole episode standing on her chair.
    Gloria Puff: Won the award that year, too. Best Live Direction, From a Chair.
    <<flag f_asked_norma>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> What's Chet like back here? <<if not flagged("f_asked_gloria_chet")>>
    Gloria Puff: He asked me to contour his TEETH, sugar. And he's been running up and down those booth stairs all night, for a man who isn't crew.
    <<flag f_asked_gloria_chet>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> Any good comebacks for Chet? <<if flagged("f_duel_known") and not flagged("f_cb_gloria")>>
    Gloria Puff: Oh, I've got one. Tell him his roots are showing. It works on everybody. Everybody has roots, sugar.
    Dex: "Your roots are showing." I'll keep it in my pocket. Though I don't remember Chet ever mentioning his hair.
    <<flag f_cb_gloria>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> How do you get into the booth? <<if not flagged("f_booth_ok") and not flagged("f_gr_ask_booth")>>
    Gloria Puff: You don't. Crew only. Norma wants a headset, a lanyard and a face she's too busy to look at.
    Gloria Puff: She's been screaming for her new runner all night. Kevin. Nobody's ever seen Kevin. Kevin might be a myth.
    <<flag f_gr_ask_booth>>
    <<jump F_GR_Gloria_Menu>>
-> Bye for now.
    Gloria Puff: Go get 'em, sugar. And don't sweat. Sweat is the enemy.
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Card
---
Gloria Puff: Mister Studwell's reserved card? Never seen it. Just like I never saw you take it.
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Sign
---
Gloria Puff: CHET IS A CHEAT. In my Scandal Red! Sugar, I'm framing that in my heart.
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Puff
---
Gloria Puff: Not near my brushes, sugar. Cheese dust is forever.
===
title: F_GR_Gloria_Nibbles
---
Gloria Puff: Is that a HAMSTER? Cute. Not my fear, sugar. Norma's, though. Ooh. Norma's.
===

title: F_GR_Booth_Look
---
Dex: A narrow door: CREW ONLY. CONTROL BOOTH. Through the little window I can see stairs going up. Next to it, an intercom with a big red TALK button.
===
title: F_GR_Booth_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_booth_ok")>>
    <<go tv_control_booth from_green_room>>
<<elseif has("runner_disguise")>>
    Dex: Headset on. Lanyard on. I press TALK and do my best tired-crew voice.
    Dex: Hey. It's, uh... Kevin. The runner.
    Norma Fade: (intercom) KEVIN! Three hours late! Get up here, I need hands!
    Dex: The door buzzes open. I'm Kevin now. Kevin has had a very long night.
    <<flag f_booth_ok>>
    <<go tv_control_booth from_green_room>>
<<elseif flagged("f_booth_refused")>>
    Norma Fade: (intercom) Still not crew. Still not Kevin. Still wearing a fruit salad. Goodbye.
    Dex: Crew wear a headset and a lanyard. And apparently they're called Kevin.
<<else>>
    Dex: I press TALK. "Hello? Can I come up?"
    Norma Fade: (intercom, crackling) Who is this? Are you crew? You're not crew. Crew have a HEADSET. Crew have a LANYARD. I can see you on the door camera. You have a SHIRT.
    Norma Fade: And crew show up on time, unlike my new runner Kevin, who I have never met and already hate. CREW ONLY!
    Dex: A headset and a lanyard. If I had both, I'd be crew. I could even be Kevin. She's never seen Kevin.
    <<flag f_booth_refused>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_GR_Booth_Half
---
<<if has("crew_headset") and has("runner_lanyard")>>
    Dex: I've got the headset and the lanyard. I should put them on together before I press TALK. Half a Kevin won't fool anybody.
<<else>>
    Dex: Half a disguise makes me half a Kevin. Norma wants a headset AND a lanyard.
<<endif>>
===

title: F_BO_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("f_booth_intro")>>
    Dex: The control booth. A wall of TV monitors, a big window looking down on the studio, about a thousand buttons, and a coffee machine that's seen things.
    Norma Fade: Kevin. FINALLY. Norma Fade, director. Rule one: don't touch anything. Rule two: don't touch ANYTHING. Rule three: coffee.
    Dex: She hasn't looked at me once. She's watching a giant countdown clock. Kevin is safe.
    <<flag f_booth_intro>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_BO_Exit_Look
---
Dex: The stairs back down to the green room. Very steep. Very Kevin-unfriendly.
===
title: F_BO_Exit_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_norma_on_chair")>>
    Norma Fade: KEVIN! DON'T YOU LEAVE ME UP HERE WITH IT!
    Dex: Be right back, boss! Getting... rodent supplies!
<<endif>>
<<go tv_green_room from_booth>>
===

title: F_BO_Monitors_Look
---
Dex: Twelve monitors. Camera one, camera two, the audience, the parking lot, and one that's just a close-up of Chet's teeth.
===
title: F_BO_Monitors_Use
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: Every monitor shows a replay of my air-guitar solo. On a loop. Norma's crying a little. I think in a good way.
<<elseif flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Dex: On monitor four, Chet is sulking. On monitor five, Roxy is fixing her lipstick. On monitor six, Lou is not smiling. A classic.
<<elseif flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Dex: Monitor four: Chet, slapping his ear and shouting "HELLO?" at nobody. Norma has turned the volume up. She's laughing. Norma laughs!
<<else>>
    Dex: Monitor four: Chet, touching his ear and nodding. Monitor nine: the little tape deck in the corner of this very booth, red light blinking, labelled CH. CHET.
    Norma Fade: Kevin. Don't touch my monitors. Look at them with less breathing.
<<endif>>
===

title: F_BO_Coffee_Look
---
Dex: A coffee maker with a handwritten sign: NORMA'S. TOUCH IT AND DIE. Under that, smaller: unless you're making me one.
===
title: F_BO_Coffee_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_made_coffee")>>
    Dex: The pot's empty. Norma drank it all in one go, like a dragon drinking a lake.
<<else>>
    Dex: I pour Norma a coffee. Black. Like her soul. I put it on her desk.
    Norma Fade: (without looking) Kevin. I could kiss you. I won't. But I could.
    <<flag f_made_coffee>>
<<endif>>
===

title: F_BO_Norma_Look
---
<<if flagged("f_norma_on_chair")>>
    Dex: Norma Fade, standing on her chair, eyes squeezed shut, holding her clipboard like a sword.
<<else>>
    Dex: Norma Fade, the director. Headset, chunky glasses, a cardigan with a pencil in every pocket, and a stopwatch round her neck she checks every four seconds.
<<endif>>
===
title: F_BO_Norma_Talk
---
<<if flagged("f_norma_on_chair")>>
    Norma Fade: KEVIN! GET! THE! RODENT! I'm not coming down until it's gone, and the show is in FOUR MINUTES!
<<elseif flagged("finale_won")>>
    Norma Fade: Kevin. Best show I've directed in thirty years. And I directed the llama episode.
<<else>>
    <<if flagged("f_made_coffee")>>
        Norma Fade: (sipping) What, Kevin? Talk fast. You've got the coffee privileges, so you've got ten seconds.
    <<else>>
        Norma Fade: What, Kevin? Talk fast. Faster. That's too fast.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_BO_Norma_Menu
---
-> What's that little tape deck in the corner? <<if not flagged("f_norma_guards") and not flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Norma Fade: That's Mister Studwell's vocal warm-up tape. Plays on a loop, on his own private channel. He says it "helps him stay in the zone".
    Norma Fade: He gave me a fruit basket. With a pineapple, Kevin. Nobody touches that deck.
    <<flag f_norma_guards>>
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
-> Do you ever leave your desk? <<if flagged("f_norma_guards") and not flagged("f_tape_swapped") and not flagged("f_norma_desk")>>
    Norma Fade: Leave my desk? Kevin, I've directed live TV through a blackout, a flood and a llama. I fear nothing. I leave for nothing.
    Norma Fade: (a speck of dust drifts past) WAS THAT A MOUSE? ...No. No, it was dust. Carry on. I fear nothing.
    <<flag f_norma_desk>>
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
-> Want me to get you a coffee? <<if not flagged("f_made_coffee")>>
    Norma Fade: Kevin, that's the first smart thing you've said. The machine's right there. Black.
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
-> Have you noticed Chet acting weird? <<if flagged("f_tape_swapped") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Norma Fade: He keeps slapping his ear and looking up here like a lost puppy. Must be nerves. Not my department. Coffee is my department.
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
-> What's the worst thing that ever happened live? <<if not flagged("f_norma_lore")>>
    Norma Fade: The llama. Don't ask about the llama. Nobody asks about the llama.
    Dex: What about the llama?
    Norma Fade: KEVIN.
    <<flag f_norma_lore>>
    <<jump F_BO_Norma_Menu>>
-> Getting back to work, boss.
    Norma Fade: Good. Be useful. Be quiet. Be Kevin.
===

title: F_BO_Deck_Look
---
<<if flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Dex: The little tape deck, empty now. Its transmitter light is off. Somewhere downstairs, Chet's earpiece is playing the sweet sound of nothing.
<<else>>
    Dex: A little tape deck wired to a transmitter with a bendy antenna. A sticky label: CH. CHET. DO NOT TOUCH. The tape inside is covered in glitter pen.
<<endif>>
===
title: F_BO_Deck_Use
---
<<if flagged("f_tape_swapped")>>
    Dex: Empty. No more whispers for Chet.
<<elseif flagged("f_norma_on_chair")>>
    Dex: Click. I pop Chet's tape out of the deck. The little red light goes dark. The label says: CHET'S COMEBACKS. PLAY ON LOOP.
    Dex: Down in the studio, faintly, I hear Chet yell: "Hello? HELLO? Copy that? ...Copy ANYTHING?"
    Dex: Professor Nibbles hops off the clipboard, gives me a tiny salute, and scampers down the stairs, straight back to Mina's pocket. A true professional.
    Norma Fade: (climbing down) Is it gone? It's gone. Thank you, Kevin. You're promoted. To Kevin.
    <<give chet_cheat_tape>>
    <<take nibbles_on_loan>>
    <<unflag f_norma_on_chair>>
    <<flag f_tape_swapped>>
<<else>>
    Norma Fade: (without turning around) Kevin. Hand. Off. The deck. That's Mister Studwell's private tape and he gave me a FRUIT BASKET.
    Dex: A recording of Chet, playing on a loop, beamed to the walkie behind Camera One, beamed into his ear. I need that tape. But not with Norma watching like a hawk.
    <<flag f_norma_guards>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_BO_Deck_PutBack
---
Dex: Put Chet's whispers back in? Absolutely not. That tape's going straight to Roxy. Eventually.
===
title: F_BO_Nibbles
---
<<if flagged("f_norma_on_chair")>>
    Dex: Nibbles is already doing his job. Beautifully.
<<else>>
    Dex: I set Professor Nibbles on the desk and give him a little nudge toward the director. Go, Professor. For science.
    Dex: Nibbles scurries across the mixing desk. Over the faders. Up Norma's clipboard. He sits on top of it and cleans his whiskers.
    Norma Fade: Is that... IS THAT A RODENT? KEVIN! KEVIN, THERE IS A RODENT ON MY CLIPBOARD!
    Dex: She's up on her chair in one jump, eyes squeezed shut. Thirty years in live TV, and this is the most alive I've ever seen anybody.
    Norma Fade: GET IT, KEVIN! DON'T JUST STAND THERE!
    Dex: On it, boss! Chasing the rodent. Totally. Near the tape deck. For no reason.
    <<flag f_norma_on_chair>>
<<endif>>
===
title: F_BO_Norma_Puff
---
Norma Fade: A cheese puff? Kevin, I'm on a diet. A coffee diet. Get that orange thing away from my buttons.
===
title: F_BO_Norma_Tape
---
Norma Fade: Music cues go in the sound board on the studio floor, Kevin. Downstairs. Where the music is. Think.
===
title: F_BO_Norma_Item
---
Norma Fade: Kevin, I don't have hands for that. I have hands for BUTTONS.
===

title: F_BO_Talkback_Look
---
Dex: The director's desk. A gooseneck microphone with a button: TALKBACK, STUDIO FLOOR. Press it and your voice comes out of every speaker downstairs.
===
title: F_BO_Talkback_Use
---
<<if flagged("finale_won")>>
    Dex: I press TALKBACK. "Goodnight, everybody." Downstairs, the whole audience says goodnight back. Lou says it last.
<<elseif flagged("f_tape_swapped") and not flagged("f_chet_busted")>>
    Dex: I could whisper lines into the studio myself... No. Feeding people lines is Chet's thing. I'll win with my own. Well, with borrowed ones. Freely given. It's different.
<<else>>
    Dex: I press TALKBACK and lean in. "Testing." Downstairs, everyone in the studio looks up at the ceiling. Lou looks at it like it owes her money.
    Norma Fade: KEVIN.
<<endif>>
===

title: F_Show
---
Roxy Vale: Five, four, three... (she mouths two, one)
Roxy Vale: GOOD EVENING, AMERICA! This is Speed Daters Live, the grand finale, coming to you LIVE!
Roxy Vale: Two men. One night. One very confused studio audience. Let's meet our finalists!
Roxy Vale: In the corner wearing the teeth, it's Chet Studwell!
Chet Studwell: (points at the camera, winks, points at himself)
Roxy Vale: And in the corner wearing every flower in Hawaii, it's Dex Dooley!
Dex: (waves) Hi, Mom. Hi, Uncle Vic. Hi, everybody I met tonight. Please don't look at me directly.
Roxy Vale: Round one: ELIMINATION! I'll call back every moment of your big night. Remember it, and you stay on. Fluff it, and you're out!
<<jump F_Elim>>
===
title: F_Elim
---
<<if has("cowboy_hat")>>
    Roxy Vale: First memory: a brown cowboy hat. Chet, whose hat is it?
    Chet Studwell: Mine. I'm a cowboy. Yee... haw? Is it yee-haw?
    Dex: It's Lacey Rae's. She only dances to real country. Hank Hollister, to be exact.
    Lacey Rae: (from the audience) THAT'S MY FRESHMAN!
<<endif>>
<<if has("bookmark")>>
    Roxy Vale: Next: a bookmark with a pressed daisy. What poem did it hold?
    Chet Studwell: "Roses Are Red, Chet Is Great."
    Dex: "Ode to the Quiet Kid in the Back Row." By Ivy.
    Ivy: (standing up, loud and clear) "I am listening. I am listening so hard."
    Dex: She said it out loud. In front of everyone. Somebody give her a medal.
<<endif>>
<<if has("sorority_pin")>>
    Roxy Vale: A sorority pin! Chet, what's the name of the sorority's flamingo?
    Chet Studwell: Flamingo... Steve?
    Dex: Fernanda. And she's back on the porch where she belongs.
    Tess Calloway: (checks a box on her clipboard) Correct, and adorable.
<<endif>>
<<if has("glow_bracelet")>>
    Roxy Vale: A glow-stick bracelet! What kept blowing the Fuse Box's fuse?
    Chet Studwell: Electricity. Next question.
    Dex: Dolly's amp. Every time she dropped the bass.
    Dolly Spark: (cranks her boombox) BWAAAM!
<<endif>>
<<if has("safety_goggles")>>
    Roxy Vale: Safety goggles! Chet, who's the Professor?
    Chet Studwell: Professor... Studwell? Me. I'm the Professor.
    Dex: Professor Nibbles. A hamster. Now a lab mascot with a very happy retirement plan.
    Dr. Mina Volt: (holding up a tiny hamster in a tiny graduation cap) He says hi!
<<endif>>
<<if has("protest_button")>>
    Roxy Vale: A protest button! Chet, what does a good protest need?
    Chet Studwell: A strongly-worded email from my dad.
    Dex: A cause, some courage, and fresh batteries.
    Sky Rivera: (megaphone) CORRECT!
<<endif>>
<<if has("diner_name_tag")>>
    Roxy Vale: A diner name tag! What did Bree need for her audition?
    Chet Studwell: A better job? Ha!
    Dex: Headshots. Her audition's tomorrow morning, and she's going to crush it.
    Bree Marlowe: (throws a napkin at Chet) Captain Coral, reporting for duty!
<<endif>>
<<if has("finished_crossword")>>
    Roxy Vale: A finished crossword! Chet, how do you make Lou smile?
    Chet Studwell: Tickets to the Chet Studwell Show?
    Dex: You don't make Lou do anything. You finish her crossword, and you wait.
    Lou: (the corner of her mouth moves one millimetre)
    Roxy Vale: Folks, that's her second smile this week. Somebody call a scientist.
<<endif>>
<<if has("white_glove")>>
    Roxy Vale: A single white glove! Mimi, would you like to give Chet a clue?
    Dex: Mimi mimes a tiny box around Chet. Then she mimes him getting smaller. And smaller. And sadder.
    Chet Studwell: Charades! Is it... me? Am I winning?
    Dex: She's saying you're trapped in a box made of your own ego.
<<endif>>
<<if has("guitar_pick")>>
    Roxy Vale: A guitar pick! Jett Vex, is this guy boring?
    Jett Vex: Bored by everything. Except him. Don't make it a thing.
<<endif>>
Roxy Vale: Final elimination question, and it's a big one. Dex, what does your Uncle Vic always say?
<<jump F_Elim_Final>>
===
title: F_Elim_Final
---
-> "Always wear a hibiscus shirt to a first date."
    Roxy Vale: Bzzzt! Sweetie, nobody would say that. Try again.
    <<jump F_Elim_Final>>
-> "Be the guy who shows up with what they need."
    Roxy Vale: Correct! And folks, he really did. Everybody in this audience got exactly what they needed tonight.
    <<jump F_Elim_Result>>
-> "Never trust a man with perfect teeth."
    Roxy Vale: Good advice, but not his! Try again, lover boy.
    Chet Studwell: Hey!
    <<jump F_Elim_Final>>
===
title: F_Elim_Result
---
Roxy Vale: Chet Studwell, without your earpiece you answered zero questions correctly.
Chet Studwell: The questions were biased! They were about things that happened!
Roxy Vale: But network rules say the finale always ends in a dance-off. Who wrote that rule?
Chet Studwell: My dad.
Roxy Vale: Who owns the network?
Chet Studwell: My dad.
Roxy Vale: Then you know what time it is. DANCE! OFF!
Dolly Spark: Hit it!
Dex: Dolly's mix starts thumping out of the speakers. Okay, feet. Don't let me down. Or do, but rhythmically.
<<jump F_Dance1>>
===
title: F_Dance1
---
Roxy Vale: Move one! Show us how you open!
Lacey Rae: (from the audience) Boots heavy, heart light, freshman!
-> Do the worm
    Dex: I drop to the floor and do the worm. Except I forget the "worm" part. I'm just lying there.
    Roxy Vale: Bold choice. Get up and try something else, sweetie.
    <<jump F_Dance1>>
-> Scoot like Lacey Rae taught me
    Dex: Heel, toe, scoot, and tip the hat. Heel, toe, scoot, and TIP THE HAT!
    Lacey Rae: YEEHAW!
    Dex: The whole front row starts line dancing. Even Lou. Okay, not Lou. But Lou's foot moved.
    <<jump F_Dance2>>
-> Moonwalk
    Dex: I try to moonwalk. I walk backwards into Camera One. The camera operator is not amused.
    Roxy Vale: Ooh, that's gonna leave a mark. Try again!
    <<jump F_Dance1>>
===
title: F_Dance2
---
Roxy Vale: Chet, your move!
Chet Studwell: Watch and learn, Dooley. The Studwell Spin!
Dex: Chet spins. And spins. And steps right into the puddle of grape soda he spilled on me earlier.
Chet Studwell: WHOAAAA!
Dex: He slides across the stage like a very expensive bowling ball. The audience gasps. Then cheers. For the puddle.
Roxy Vale: Dex! Move two! Make it big!
-> Pretend to be stuck in an invisible box
    Dex: I put my palms up against a wall that isn't there. I push. I find a door. I open it. I'm free!
    Dex: In the audience, Mimi stands up and mimes slow clapping. A mime's standing ovation. Silent and beautiful.
    <<jump F_Dance3>>
-> Do the robot
    Dex: I do the robot. A robot that needs new batteries. Mina shakes her head sadly.
    Roxy Vale: Low power, lover boy! Try again!
    <<jump F_Dance2>>
-> Shout "LOOK OVER THERE!" and run away
    Dex: Everyone looks over there. There's nothing there. Everyone looks back at me. I'm still here.
    Roxy Vale: Nice try. Dance!
    <<jump F_Dance2>>
===
title: F_Dance3
---
Roxy Vale: Final move! Make it count!
Jett Vex: (from the audience) Don't get lame now, Dooley!
-> Bow politely and sit down
    Dex: I bow. The audience waits. Jett yawns, very loudly, on purpose.
    Roxy Vale: Not yet, lover boy! Big finish!
    <<jump F_Dance3>>
-> Slide into an air-guitar solo on my knees
    Dex: I drop to my knees, slide all the way across the stage, and shred the loudest air guitar in television history.
    Jett Vex: ...Okay. That was NOT boring.
    Dex: Jett throws her arms in the air. The whole audience is on its feet. Ivy is screaming. IVY is SCREAMING.
    <<jump F_Call>>
-> Copy Chet's spin
    Dex: I try the Studwell Spin. I spin. I get dizzy. I see three Roxys. All three of them look disappointed.
    Roxy Vale: Be yourself, sweetie! Again!
    <<jump F_Dance3>>
===
title: F_Call
---
Roxy Vale: Hold on, folks, we have a caller on the line! Caller, you're live on Speed Daters Live!
Uncle Vic: (on the phone) Is this thing on? Dexter? It's your Uncle Vic!
Dex: Uncle Vic?! You're watching?
Uncle Vic: The whole retirement home is watching, kid. Mrs. Pomeroy fainted during the air guitar. In a good way.
Uncle Vic: I told you to be the guy who shows up with what they need. I didn't know you'd do it for the whole city in one night.
Uncle Vic: I'm proud of you, Dexter. Now win the thing. I've got twenty bucks on you with Mrs. Pomeroy.
Dex: Thanks, Uncle Vic. I love you. Please don't call me Dexter on TV.
Uncle Vic: Love you too, Dexter!
<<jump F_Win>>
===
title: F_Win
---
Roxy Vale: The votes are in! The audience voted, the judges voted, and Mrs. Pomeroy voted twice!
Roxy Vale: The winner of Speed Daters Live is... DEX DOOLEY!
Dex: Confetti. So much confetti. Lacey Rae is yodelling. Sky is chanting. Mimi is miming fireworks. Tess has already made a banner.
Chet Studwell: This is rigged! ...Wait, no, that was me. Never mind.
Roxy Vale: Dex, you've won the grand prize: a dream date with anyone you choose! So, lover boy, who's it gonna be?
-> Everybody. Group date at the diner. Bree's section.
    Bree Marlowe: I'll push some tables together!
    Lou: I'll bring my own drinks.
    Roxy Vale: Ten dates at once? That's not a date, that's a parade. I love it!
-> Roxy, obviously.
    Roxy Vale: Oh, honey. I'm the host. I'm married to the show. But I'm flattered.
    Roxy Vale: Pick everybody. It's what you do best.
    Dex: Then everybody it is! Group date at the diner!
-> Can I take Uncle Vic?
    Uncle Vic: (still on the line) I accept!
    Roxy Vale: Okay, Uncle Vic AND everybody. Diner. Group date. Go!
Dex: When I signed up for this show I didn't have a talent, a partner, or a clue.
Dex: Now I've got a cowboy hat, a pocket full of keepsakes, and a whole audience full of friends.
Dex: Turns out you don't have to be the smoothest guy in the room. You just have to show up with what people need.
Roxy Vale: That's our show! Goodnight, everybody! Goodnight, lover boy!
<<flag finale_won>>
Dex: THE END.
Dex: (Thanks for playing Big Night Out! Stick around: the studio is still open, and Roxy has a few more things to say.)
===


title: Item_lapel_mic_Look
---
<<if has("nine_volt")>>
    Dex: A wireless mic pack with an empty battery slot. And I've got a nine-volt right here.
<<else>>
    Dex: A wireless mic pack. Battery slot: empty. A mic with no power. Like me before coffee.
<<endif>>
===
title: Item_nine_volt_Look
---
Dex: A nine-volt battery from Sky's megaphone. I lick it to check. Yep. Ow. Yep.
===
title: Item_soda_water_Look
---
Dex: A bottle of club soda from Lou's bag. The bubbles are the only cheerful thing about it.
===
title: Item_cocktail_napkin_Look
---
Dex: A napkin from Bree's apron. "Blot, don't rub," she said. Bree knows things.
===
title: Item_studio_walkie_Look
---
Dex: A walkie-talkie with CHET on it in glitter pen, set to channel CHET. Its little screen says RECEIVING FROM: BOOTH. Subtle, Chet.
===
title: Item_chet_mixtape_Look
---
<<if flagged("f_tape_wound")>>
    Dex: "Chet's Pump-Up Jams, Volume 9: Songs About Chet." Wound back in and ready to be recorded over. Please.
<<else>>
    Dex: "Chet's Pump-Up Jams, Volume 9: Songs About Chet." Half the tape is hanging out of it like brown spaghetti.
<<endif>>
===
title: Item_floor_fillers_tape_Look
---
Dex: "Dolly's Floor-Fillers, Dex Edition." Written over Chet's label in glitter. Chet's own glitter pen, probably.
===
title: Item_reserved_card_Look
---
Dex: A stiff white card: RESERVED: C. STUDWELL. ALL NIGHT. The back is totally blank. Perfect for writing on.
===
title: Item_scandal_lipstick_Look
---
Dex: Gloria's Scandal Red lipstick. Discontinued for being too scandalous. It's a very bold red. It could write a very bold sentence.
===
title: Item_chet_protest_sign_Look
---
Dex: CHET IS A CHEAT, in big Scandal Red letters on the back of his own RESERVED card. With a drawing of his teeth. Art.
===
title: Item_runner_lanyard_Look
---
Dex: A blue crew lanyard: CREW: KEVIN. ALL ACCESS. Kevin never picked it up. Kevin, wherever you are, I'm sorry. And thank you.
===
title: Item_dolly_headphones_Look
---
Dex: Dolly's big turquoise DJ headphones. Real crew headsets have a little microphone arm in front of your mouth, though. These need something thin and bendy.
===
title: Item_bendy_straw_Look
---
Dex: A pink bendy straw. Bendy straws make everything a party. And they bend into very convincing shapes.
===
title: Item_crew_headset_Look
---
Dex: Dolly's headphones with a bendy straw for a microphone arm. From a distance, I'm crew. From up close, I'm a guy with a straw on his face.
===
title: Item_runner_disguise_Look
---
Dex: The Kevin Kit: homemade headset plus Kevin's lanyard. Wearing it, I feel underpaid and slightly tired. Very convincing.
===
title: Item_studio_cheese_puff_Look
---
Dex: One neon-orange cheese puff. No natural food is this colour. Hamsters go wild for it, apparently.
===
title: Item_nibbles_on_loan_Look
---
Dex: Professor Nibbles, in a paper cup, on loan from Mina. He's wearing a look of total professional focus. Also cheese dust.
===
title: Item_chet_cheat_tape_Look
---
Dex: "CHET'S COMEBACKS. PLAY ON LOOP. CHANNEL CHET." In glitter pen. The proof Chet's been cheating all season.
===
title: Item_bun_pencil_Look
---
Dex: Bree's order pencil, still warm from her bun. Ten thousand orders taken. Its eraser is just a memory. It would fit perfectly in a cassette's little hole.
===
